NOT REDISTRIBUTED
No TI MCU+ SDK code is included or linked. boards/lp-am243x uses a local SDK
installation for its prebuilt boot loader and its image-signing and flashing
scripts only; those remain under Texas Instruments' license.

startup.S brings the core up the way that SDK's nortos kernel does, because
that kernel builds only with TI Arm Clang. It is a reimplementation and not a
copy: the MPU is programmed by a table-driven loop where the SDK has a C layer
over named assembly functions, and the data cache is invalidated with the
architectural set/way sequence where the SDK uses the Cortex-R5's
single-instruction c15, c5, 0. What does come from TI material is
configuration data rather than code - the five MPU region values SysConfig
generates for this board, the UART0 base address and its register offsets, and
the memory ranges in am243x_r5f.lds.in. Those are facts about the chip, out of
its technical reference manual. The eight-entry vector table is the shape
ARMv7-R mandates, in the order the architecture fixes.
